{"packet_id":"D069-01","doc_id":"D069","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Forbidding the Algorithmic Inflation of Rent (FAIR) Act","requirement":"Makes it unlawful for rental property owners, agents, and coordinators to use, subscribe to, or perform algorithmic coordinating functions that use competitors' competitively sensitive information to set or recommend rents, or to engage in parallel pricing coordination. Municipalities may not enact conflicting ordinances.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applies to rental property owners of one or more residential dwelling units, coordinators, agents, representatives, and subcontractors. Excludes government entities using affordability controls, and certain research, public estimates, and brokerage databases.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Applies to rental property owners, coordinators, and any person performing a coordinating function or parallel pricing coordination."},"exemptions":"Government entities setting rents through affordability controls; research/statistical analysis not used for pricing; free public rent estimates; real estate brokerage databases available equally to subscribers; spreadsheets without AI; databases used only for queries.","penalty":"Violation is unlawful under the New Jersey Antitrust Act; remedies and penalties of that Act (P.L.1970, c.73, §§ 6-17) apply.","effective_date":"2027-07-01","citation":"P.L. 2026, c. 43, § 4","quoted_span":"4.    It
shall be unlawful and a violation of the “New Jersey Antitrust Act,” P.L.1970,
c.73 (C.56:9-1 et seq.) for:
a.     a rental property owner, or any agent,
representative, or subcontractor thereof, to receive, subscribe to, contract
for, or otherwise exchange any form of consideration in return for the use of,
the services of a coordinator;","interaction":"Supplements the New Jersey Antitrust Act; municipalities prohibited from enacting conflicting ordinances.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
